So this is just
the original audio.

01:23:12.910 --> 01:23:13.577
[AUDIO PLAYBACK]

01:23:13.577 --> 01:23:14.997
(SINGING) I want
to be the very--

01:23:14.997 --> 01:23:15.580
[END PLAYBACK]

01:23:15.580 --> 01:23:16.750
OK.

01:23:16.750 --> 01:23:19.780
And so first, let's look at
what the low-frequency cut off

01:23:19.780 --> 01:23:22.150
version of this
audio looks like.

01:23:22.150 --> 01:23:23.510
The audio is coming from here.

01:23:23.510 --> 01:23:24.800
OK.

01:23:24.800 --> 01:23:27.590
[MUFFLED AUDIO]

01:23:28.090 --> 01:23:30.197
(SINGING) I want
be the very best--

01:23:30.197 --> 01:23:30.780
[END PLAYBACK]

01:23:30.780 --> 01:23:32.400
OK, so you observe that.

01:23:32.400 --> 01:23:35.040
OK, it still was
like the [INAUDIBLE]

01:23:35.040 --> 01:23:39.030
wants to be the very best, but
somehow very dull about it.

01:23:39.030 --> 01:23:40.800
We remove the
high-frequency components.

01:23:40.800 --> 01:23:42.300
It sounded very dull.

01:23:42.300 --> 01:23:44.520
OK, so that's one way
to do lossy compression.

01:23:44.520 --> 01:23:47.790
But I could also just reduce the
number of quantization levels,

01:23:47.790 --> 01:23:49.320
keep all the frequencies.

01:23:49.320 --> 01:23:51.311
Let's do that next.

01:23:51.311 --> 01:23:54.038
[AUDIO PLAYBACK]

01:23:54.538 --> 01:23:57.890
(SINGING) I want
to be the very best

01:23:57.890 --> 01:23:58.390
No--

01:23:58.390 --> 01:23:58.973
[END PLAYBACK]

01:23:58.973 --> 01:24:00.940
OK, so in this
case, you can hear

01:24:00.940 --> 01:24:03.035
all the instruments and
the high-frequency stuff,

01:24:03.035 --> 01:24:03.910
the treble, the bass.

01:24:03.910 --> 01:24:06.730
But there was a very
static noise behind.

01:24:06.730 --> 01:24:07.780
There was like sh-sh-ch.

01:24:07.780 --> 01:24:08.950
Let's just hear it quickly.

01:24:08.950 --> 01:24:09.617
[AUDIO PLAYBACK]

01:24:09.617 --> 01:24:11.307
(SINGING) No one ever was--

01:24:11.307 --> 01:24:11.890
[END PLAYBACK]

01:24:11.890 --> 01:24:14.720
It's like shh-sh-sh
kind of going on.

01:24:14.720 --> 01:24:16.550
So that's basically
being introduced

01:24:16.550 --> 01:24:19.160
because now you have increased
the quantization level.

01:24:19.160 --> 01:24:22.790
So you see how playing with
these two different knobs

01:24:22.790 --> 01:24:25.640
led to different distortion
in some sense, very

01:24:25.640 --> 01:24:28.010
different sounding distortion.

01:24:28.010 --> 01:24:32.060
But what you can do is like
you can go ahead and plot it

01:24:32.060 --> 01:24:35.120
as the rate distortion curves
which we have looked at before.

01:24:35.120 --> 01:24:38.330
So on the x-axis is rate,
y-axis is distortion.

01:24:38.330 --> 01:24:42.140
And we are playing with-- we
are doing many different colors

01:24:42.140 --> 01:24:43.850
at different frequency cutoffs.

01:24:43.850 --> 01:24:47.180
Different symbols are
different quantization level.

01:24:47.180 --> 01:24:49.130
And this is what people
also do in practice.

01:24:49.130 --> 01:24:51.392
You would actually-- this
is what I was saying.

01:24:51.392 --> 01:24:52.850
If you are a
streaming service, you

01:24:52.850 --> 01:24:54.380
will actually
encode this Pokemon

01:24:54.380 --> 01:24:57.020
in various of these forms.

01:24:57.020 --> 01:25:00.200
And you will basically keep the
points which give you the lowest

01:25:00.200 --> 01:25:02.090
distortion at any given rate.

01:25:02.090 --> 01:25:05.590
So what you will see
here is at low bitrate--

01:25:05.590 --> 01:25:07.340
you can't see whatever
I am drawing there.

01:25:07.340 --> 01:25:09.740
OK, so at low bitrate
you have colors,

01:25:09.740 --> 01:25:13.980
which are changing whereas at
high bitrates, like the things.

01:25:13.980 --> 01:25:16.650
So this black dot is the
perito optimal black line.

01:25:16.650 --> 01:25:19.318
You see, the number
of quantization levels

01:25:19.318 --> 01:25:19.860
are changing.

01:25:19.860 --> 01:25:21.330
This symbols are changing.

01:25:21.330 --> 01:25:25.020
So what's really happening is
that at extremely low rate,

01:25:25.020 --> 01:25:29.480
you are benefiting by including
more and more frequencies.

01:25:29.480 --> 01:25:31.700
But after a point,
it doesn't really

01:25:31.700 --> 01:25:34.310
matter to include that more
frequency because that anyways

01:25:34.310 --> 01:25:35.030
has low energy.

01:25:35.030 --> 01:25:38.090
You can just throw it
away, rather really

01:25:38.090 --> 01:25:40.700
keep the frequencies, which
are low and much, much

01:25:40.700 --> 01:25:42.530
higher fidelity.

01:25:42.530 --> 01:25:45.050
So this is like this--

01:25:45.050 --> 01:25:46.850
every streaming
service has these

01:25:46.850 --> 01:25:49.250
are called encoding tables.

01:25:49.250 --> 01:25:52.130
And you will have some
version of this people playing

01:25:52.130 --> 01:25:54.440
with these knobs in
practice to figure out

01:25:54.440 --> 01:25:57.035
what's the optimal way
to compress my symbol.

01:26:00.590 --> 01:26:06.410
And so this was like we did some
transform and then quantized.

01:26:06.410 --> 01:26:08.270
But let's say your
friend who never

01:26:08.270 --> 01:26:11.420
took this class actually
didn't transform,

01:26:11.420 --> 01:26:12.860
he directly quantized.

01:26:12.860 --> 01:26:15.980
So this is similar to the
example which we looked above.

01:26:15.980 --> 01:26:20.960
In that case, basically you
get these black dots, which

01:26:20.960 --> 01:26:22.610
are much higher in distortion.

01:26:22.610 --> 01:26:26.840
So now you can see for basically
similar power of quantization,

01:26:26.840 --> 01:26:29.360
you get much higher
distortion compared

01:26:29.360 --> 01:26:31.430
to if you were doing
transform coding.

01:26:31.430 --> 01:26:34.460
I think there was an example.

01:26:34.460 --> 01:26:35.870
OK, maybe I missed this, sorry.

01:26:35.870 --> 01:26:36.930
So the shh.

01:26:36.930 --> 01:26:37.430
[INAUDIBLE]

01:26:37.430 --> 01:26:39.740
Yeah.

01:26:39.740 --> 01:26:40.610
OK, yeah.

01:26:40.610 --> 01:26:45.350
So yep, I think
this is an example.

01:26:45.350 --> 01:26:48.340
Let's just hear it.

01:26:48.340 --> 01:26:49.680
[AUDIO PLAYBACK]

01:26:49.680 --> 01:26:50.180
Sorry?

01:26:50.180 --> 01:26:50.460
Yeah.

01:26:50.460 --> 01:26:52.620
That is the low-pass and the
one bellow is direct pass?

01:26:52.620 --> 01:26:53.220
Exactly.

01:26:53.220 --> 01:26:55.320
So this is, again,
the low-pass one.

01:26:55.320 --> 01:26:56.730
So we transform and quantize.

01:26:56.730 --> 01:26:59.724
And the next one is
just direct quantized.

01:26:59.724 --> 01:27:02.184
[AUDIO PLAYBACK]

01:27:02.184 --> 01:27:03.237
(SINGING) I want to be--

01:27:03.237 --> 01:27:03.820
[END PLAYBACK]

01:27:03.820 --> 01:27:05.110
OK.

01:27:05.110 --> 01:27:07.030
And this is the second one.

01:27:07.030 --> 01:27:09.862
[AUDIO PLAYBACK]

01:27:10.806 --> 01:27:13.357
(SINGING) I want
to be the very best

01:27:13.357 --> 01:27:13.940
[END PLAYBACK]

01:27:13.940 --> 01:27:17.190
OK, so here I tricked you
because both of these symbols

01:27:17.190 --> 01:27:19.140
basically have the same MSC.

01:27:19.140 --> 01:27:23.490
So they roughly sounded similar,
but if you look at the bitrate,

01:27:23.490 --> 01:27:27.060
the direct quantization
one took 160 kbps.

01:27:27.060 --> 01:27:28.080
So it's here.

01:27:28.080 --> 01:27:31.680
It took 160 kbps, whereas
transform plus quantize one

01:27:31.680 --> 01:27:33.510
took just 86.

01:27:33.510 --> 01:27:37.380
So similar sounding, but
transform clearly helps.

01:27:37.380 --> 01:27:39.750
And just the last thing
which I want to show.

01:27:39.750 --> 01:27:43.710
And I'll end the lecture here
is, OK, this was a bare bones

01:27:43.710 --> 01:27:44.490
lossy compressor.

01:27:44.490 --> 01:27:45.930
It was literally that pipeline.

01:27:45.930 --> 01:27:46.920
We did the DCT.

01:27:46.920 --> 01:27:49.770
We did some quantization,
and we worked around,

01:27:49.770 --> 01:27:52.980
but there is a very
popular compressor, MP3.

01:27:52.980 --> 01:27:55.830
So we might want to compare
how our compressor performs

01:27:55.830 --> 01:27:58.100
with respect to MP3.

